==English==
{{slim-wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|clene}}, {{m|enm|clane}}, from {{inh|en|ang|clǣne|t=clean, pure}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*klaini}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*klainiz|t=shining, fine, splendid, tender}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*glēy-|t=gleaming}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gel-|t=to gleam}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|sco|clean|t=absolute, pure, clear, empty}} and {{m|sco|clene}}, {{m|sco|clane|t=clean}}, {{cog|frr|klien|t=small}}, {{cog|nl|klein|t=small}}, {{cog|nds|kleen|t=small}}, {{cog|de|klein|t=small}}, {{cog|sv|klen|t=weak, feeble, delicate}}, {{cog|is|klénn|t=poor, feeble, petty, snug, puny, cheesy, lame}}.

