===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[remove]] [[dirt]] from a place or object.
#: {{ux|en|Can you '''clean''' the windows today?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[tidy]] up, make a place [[neat]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Clean''' your room right now!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|climbing}} To remove [[equipment]] from a climbing route after it was previously lead climbed.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make things clean in general.
#: {{ux|en|She just likes to '''clean'''. That’s why I married her.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To remove unnecessary [[file]]s, etc. from (a [[directory]], etc.).
# {{lb|en|intransitive|curling}} To [[brush]] the [[ice]] lightly in front of a moving [[rock]] to remove any [[debris]] and ensure a correct [[line]]; less vigorous than a [[sweep]].
# {{lb|en|manga|_|fandom}} To purge a [[raw]] of any blemishes caused by the [[scan]]ning process such as brown tinting and poor color contrast.
# {{lb|en|video games}} {{synonym of|en|clean up}}
# To remove guts and/or scales of a butchered animal.

